{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<p class="crumb"><a href="{{backUrl}}">&larr; Content</a></p>
<h1>Import &amp; export</h1>
<p class="hint">Every page and every template as one JSON file. {{pages}} page(s),
  {{templateCount}} template(s). Each row carries a <em>merge key</em> stamped once and never
  changed, so bringing a bundle back is a merge rather than a pile of duplicates &mdash; whatever a
  page's address has become since.</p>

<h2>Take it away</h2>
<div class="doing"><a class="btn" href="{{bundleUrl}}" download>Download everything</a></div>
<p class="hint">Drafts and the pages locked away from AI are in it, which is why this needs the
  permission that writes pages rather than the one that reads them. Keep it in git, hand it to
  somebody, or restore from it.</p>

<h2>Bring one back</h2>
{{^canImport}}<p class="hint">Importing writes pages <em>and</em> puts them live, so it needs
  &ldquo;publish pages&rdquo; as well as &ldquo;write pages&rdquo;. You have one of the two.</p>{{/canImport}}
{{#canImport}}
<form method="post" action="{{uploadUrl}}" enctype="multipart/form-data">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="bundle" value="1">
  <div class="field"><label for="b-file">a bundle from a file</label>
    <input id="b-file" type="file" name="file" accept=".json,application/json" required></div>
  <div class="doing"><button type="submit">Bring it in</button>
    <button type="button" class="quiet" data-modal="paste">or paste one</button></div>
</form>

<dialog id="paste" class="picker">
  <form method="post" action="{{action}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="import">
    <h2>Paste a bundle</h2>
    <div class="field"><label for="b-json">the JSON</label>
      <textarea id="b-json" name="bundle" rows="12" placeholder="{ &quot;hearth&quot;: 1, &quot;content&quot;: [ ... ] }"></textarea></div>
    <div class="doing"><button type="submit">Bring it in</button>
      <button type="button" class="quiet" data-close>Cancel</button></div>
  </form>
</dialog>

<p class="hint"><strong>Only what differs is written.</strong> A page whose every field matches is
  skipped entirely &mdash; no save, no event, no version &mdash; so pushing the whole site on every
  commit does not fill the history with edits nobody made. A key this site has never seen arriving
  at an address already taken is <em>adopted</em> rather than duplicated, and a row with no key at
  all still imports and is given one.</p>
<p class="hint">Every page an import writes is versioned like any other edit, so an import that went
  wrong is undone from a page's history rather than from a backup.</p>
{{/canImport}}

<h2>From a script</h2>
<p class="hint">The same thing over HTTP, which is what a command line tool uses. It answers with
  what changed, row by row, and <code>?dry=1</code> answers the same thing without writing.</p>
<pre><code>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" {{apiUrl}} &gt; site.json

curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
     --data-binary @site.json "{{apiUrl}}?dry=1"</code></pre>
{{#apiPage}}<p class="hint">A token is made on <a href="{{.}}">your programs page</a>.</p>{{/apiPage}}
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
